        "question_type": "Objective",
        "exam_year": "2000",
        "question_text": "<p>If $\\sin \\theta = \\frac{3}{5}$, find $\\cos \\theta$ in a right-angled triangle.</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>Using the Pythagorean identity, $\\sin^2 \\theta + \\cos^2 \\theta = 1$. Thus, $\\cos \\theta = \\sqrt{1 - \\sin^2 \\theta} = \\sqrt{1 - \\left(\\frac{3}{5}\\right)^2} = \\sqrt{\\frac{16}{25}} = \\frac{4}{5}$.</p>",
